cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this package, please cite both the package and the methods paper it implements."
title: "eiod: Intake dietary environmental impact metrics for Stata"
abstract: >-
  A Stata implementation of the absolute threshold, relative benchmark and
  composite dietary environmental impact metrics defined in Intake's
  Environmental Impacts of Diets methods paper. The package implements the
  published metric cut-offs; it does not contain the Environmental Impacts of
  Foods database. A companion R implementation is available as reiod.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Nicholus Tint"
    family-names: "Zaw"
    email: "nicholustintzaw@gmail.com"
    affiliation: "International Food Policy Research Institute (IFPRI)"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-14
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/nicholustintzaw/eiod"
url: "https://nicholustintzaw.github.io/eiod/"
keywords:
  - Stata
  - dietary assessment
  - environmental impact
  - planetary health
  - sustainable diets
  - food systems
references:
  - type: report
    title: "Methods for Assessing Healthy, Environmentally Sustainable Diets Globally"
    authors:
      - name: "Intake - Center for Dietary Assessment"
    year: 2026
    url: "https://www.intake.org/sites/default/files/2026-01/Intake-EIOD-Methods-Paper-Jan2026-Final.pdf"
    notes: >-
      Source of the metric definitions and of every cut-off value shipped in
      functions/dta/. The preferred citation form has been put to Intake and
      this entry will be updated when they reply.
  - type: software
    title: "reiod: Dietary Environmental Impact Metrics from the Intake EIOD Framework"
    authors:
      - given-names: "Nicholus Tint"
        family-names: "Zaw"
    notes: "The companion R implementation. Both read the same cut-off CSV."
    repository-code: "https://github.com/nicholustintzaw/reiod"
